{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994839129288001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"jinx-node-mudra","assignee":"Joe Oakhart","author":"Joe Oakhart","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":5},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1783111567012358001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"68586368-43b7-47f4-9492-8bdb3cb075fe","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6ae5-6307-e7c8-4d61"}],"description":"# e2e editor test `test_editor_batch_library_select_and_author` fails on main (authored criterion not referenced)\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n1. From a checkout of `main` (verified at `d42afd880`), with Node/npm available locally:\n2. `python -m pytest tests/e2e/test_editor_batch_library.py::test_editor_batch_library_select_and_author`\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n- **Expected:** after the editor's batch AUTHOR flow creates a new criterion (`my-new-crit`),\n  the batch step's first criterion references it: `authored[\"batch\"][\"criteria\"][0][\"prompt\"] == \"my-new-crit\"`.\n- **Actual:** the step still references the pre-existing criteria — `[{'prompt': 'tests'},\n  {'prompt': 'ticket-quality', 'when': ...}]`; assertion fails `'tests' == 'my-new-crit'`\n  (`tests/e2e/test_editor_batch_library.py:99`).\n\n## Notes\n- **Pre-existing on `main`** — reproduces identically with and without the item-15 llm reorg\n  (change 238), so it is NOT caused by that change. Discovered while running the full suite for\n  ITEM 15 (toll-clock-tier).\n- Does not block the gating Gerrit CI (the `not integration and not external` default suite): the\n  `e2e` tier self-skips when Node/npm is absent, so the CI image does not exercise it (which is\n  how it reached `main`). It DOES fail locally where Node is present.\n- Likely in the editor-server batch-author path (`llm/workflow/editor_server.py` /\n  `prompt_library` write + criterion-reference wiring), not the prompt reorg.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Root-cause why the authored criterion id is not written onto the batch step's first criterion.\n- [ ] `test_editor_batch_library_select_and_author` passes locally (with Node present) and in CI.\n- [ ] Confirm the `e2e` tier's CI skip behavior is intended (or wire Node into the gate so e2e regressions are caught).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b96ac3e4-6f59-4456-8cd3-38bcd7b5cc95","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fe55-1471-3819-44c7","ticket_type":"bug","title":"e2e editor batch-author test fails on main: authored criterion not referenced","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c37c6790-82b8-40d6-9331-350c13899ae7","68586368-43b7-47f4-9492-8bdb3cb075fe","b96ac3e4-6f59-4456-8cd3-38bcd7b5cc95","762e4296-6b2c-4a45-bf08-fb6563d76874","504f674d-3ceb-4f6c-8d03-7de023346052"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994839129288001,"uuid":"affc285d-4342-4f41-9bdd-f233e49b6ef9"}